// # Scan Subsystem Anchor - Bytes Arriving Into Whole Lines
//
// Logline: Buffers partial reads into complete lines so output never splits one.
//
// Setup: Skeleton. Pure; mirrors std/net/varlink/frame.oo, which owns this shape.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Emit whole lines only, holding any trailing partial line for later.
//   2. Reassemble correctly across non-ASCII content and missing final newline.
// No implementation yet. This anchor is the documented landing zone for the
// scan pages and gives `make verify` a page to check in this domain.
//
// A read boundary is not a line boundary, and char_at is O(index) so scanning a
// long file character by character is quadratic. Take the read offset from the
// caller rather than seeking, so a rotation cannot rewind progress behind its back.
//
// First page to write: scan_take_line.oo, mirroring varlink_frame_push. Reusing
// that page's shape is deliberate; two line assemblers will disagree.
